Scripts that I find useful for SiB4.

ccdonesib, cchecksib, and ccnumsib
----------------------------------
Scripts to check to see if a SiB4 simulation is finished running.


ccrunsibg and ccrunsibs
------------------------
Scripts to start running a SiB4 simulation, using multiple processors.


exportgcc, exportifort, and exportpgi
-------------------------------------
Scripts to set the environmental library,
  used for running SiB4 with different compilers.
  -Assumes bash
  -To utilize, preface with source:
    >source exportgcc


myhsibcopy, mypsibcopy, myqsibcopy
-----------------------------------
Script to compress netcdf output using nccopy.


rename_file
-----------
A perl script to change the names of files.
For example, to change text in all files in
a directory, you can use:
>rename_file -t -r "xxx" -w "xxx" file (-t=test)
where the -t is for testing (take out to replace),
      the -r is the text that will be replaced
  and the -w is the text that will now be seen


sib4_taryr.pl
--------------
A perl script to tar individual years of output.


